{"severity":"error","file":"errors/role_grant_exceeded_1.march","start_line":30,"start_col":12,"end_line":30,"end_col":22,"message":"The body of role `Cons` writes a file, but the role is granted only `Cap(IO.Console)` (`role Cons needs IO.Console`). A role's grant bounds everything its code reaches, as `main`'s grant bounds the program.\nhelp: add `IO.FileWrite` to the grant in protocol `Stream`: `role Cons needs IO.Console, IO.FileWrite`. The body then takes one `Cap` per granted capability, in the grant's order, between the session capability and the state, so it gains a parameter: `fn (s, cap_console, cap_file_write, st) -> ...`. Pass `cap_file_write` on to any function the body hands its capabilities to. Or remove the use.","code":"role_grant_exceeded","fix":null,"labels":[{"file":"errors/role_grant_exceeded_1.march","start_line":42,"start_col":25,"end_line":42,"end_col":29,"message":"the body calls `cons` here"},{"file":"errors/role_grant_exceeded_1.march","start_line":36,"start_col":6,"end_line":36,"end_col":10,"message":"`cons` calls `save` here"},{"file":"errors/role_grant_exceeded_1.march","start_line":42,"start_col":6,"end_line":42,"end_col":41,"message":"the body of role `Cons`, passed to `Stream_Run.run_Cons`"},{"file":"errors/role_grant_exceeded_1.march","start_line":18,"start_col":4,"end_line":18,"end_col":30,"message":"role `Cons` is granted only `Cap(IO.Console)` here"}],"notes":[],"category":"CAPABILITY"}
{"severity":"error","file":"errors/role_grant_exceeded_1.march","start_line":30,"start_col":12,"end_line":30,"end_col":22,"message":"`file_write` is internal to the standard library; use `File.write`.","code":"stdlib_internal","fix":{"kind":"replace","start_line":30,"start_col":12,"end_line":30,"end_col":50,"text":"Authority.must(File.write(\"/tmp/n\", int_to_string(n)))","applicability":"machine-applicable"},"labels":[],"notes":[],"category":"PROGRAM"}
